{
 "about": "The plate register: one permanent catalog number for every isoscape design. A plate never changes when a design is redrawn (that is its version) and is never reused, even if a design is withdrawn. Printed form uses a middle dot (STC·02); data and filenames use a hyphen (STC-02). See \"Plates\" in the README.",
 "scheme": {
  "plate": "<SET>-<NN>: the set's three-letter code, then the piece's number within the set",
  "numbers": "two digits, given in order of first release within the set and never reused; a set of boxes uses its box numbers, 00 for the set sheet (the framed menu of boxes) and M for its map",
  "taxonomy": "isoscape › collection › set › piece. A collection or set can be renamed without changing any plate.",
  "kind": "optional, per plate: what sort of piece it is (\"Map\", \"Landmark\", \"Building cutaway\"), printed as one line of the title block; absent prints nothing"
 },
 "collections": [
  {
